== 27-12 The Bohr Model

- Bohr postulated that electrons in orbit would not radiate energy, contradicting classical physics
- In the Bohr model, a single photon of light is emitted only when an electron jumps from a higher to a lower energy state

$ h f = E_u - E_ell $

- Bohr found that his theory would agree with Balmer formula if the angular momentum $L$ of the electron was _quantized_ and was an integer $n$ times $h/(2pi)$. Then by $L = I omega = (m r^2) (v / r) = m v r$, his quantum condition is $L = m v r_n$

